Id: sctl002w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set kern.sugid_coredump=0 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl.conf(5); sysctl(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

kern.sugid_coredump is 1, so a set-user-ID or set-group-ID program
that crashes dumps core its user can read. The dump holds what the
program had in memory, which for such a program may be another user's
data, a password or a key. FreeBSD refuses these dumps unless told
otherwise:
  # sysctl -w kern.sugid_coredump=0
and keep it in /etc/sysctl.conf.
